WEBVTT

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.510
Where the Sun Shines

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.260
SHOGI HALL

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:38.260
Hey, Kiriyama!

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:39.760
WAVE
WAVE

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:41.010
Over here! You got a moment?

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.520
Here, have a seat.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.060
Kishou Yanagihara. Good evening.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:52.940
Hey, Kiriyama.
Congrats on becoming the Newcomer King.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.530
Thank you.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.950
KABUKI AGESEN

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.200
A commemoration match?

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.160
With Meijin Souya?

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.550
<i>Just saying his name out loud</i>

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.140
<i>gave me goose bumps.</i>

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:32.860
<i>In our country, he's the child of God.</i>

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:43.450
Um, it won't be at the Shogi Hall, as usual?

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.750
Usually we do. But this year is different!

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.130
We'll invite people, get the press to cover it,

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:54.380
and make it a huge event!
Like boom, bam!

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.800
In fact, on the same level as a title match.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:07.850
But, um, why make such a...
Why so suddenly?

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.310
Speaking frankly, Kiriyama,

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.310
you're aware of cases

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:15.690
for the person who becomes the
Newcomer King goes on to become a meijin?

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.190
I won it before.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:18.700
So did I.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:22.120
And then, you're the fifth
middle school student in shogi history

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.780
to become a professional right after Souya.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:30.290
Everybody's rooting for you
to become a meijin too, Kiriyama.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:34.420
A star showdown!
The current meijin versus the future meijin!

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.760
<i>How can he say that so lightly?!</i>

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:40.130
But unlike our era,
you've got Souya to contend with,

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:43.800
so I feel sorry for you young guys.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.930
Yeah. He wasn't around in our day.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:50.640
Yep. Sure am glad I was born
a long time ago. Kidding.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.900
Still, he used to be cute.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.270
Back when Souya won his first title.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.490
He's already an old man now.

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:01.530
Hey, Souya's no old man.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:03.110
Sure he is.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.830
I mean, he's the same age as Shimada.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.960
Well, it's a mystery
how those two could be the same age.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:17.960
I know. What the hell happened
in Shimada's life?

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.550
SHINY SHINY

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.550
DIM...

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.510
I would swear that
Shimada's the same age as Gotou.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:27.350
But Shimada's still in his 30s, right?

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.230
Um, can we change the subject?

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:34.400
Anyway, what are we going to do
about this year's Kishou championship?

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.940
My plan was to bill it as, "Sakurai 7th-Dan
taking on his first title championship!"

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.940
Shogi Association's Mountaineering Club

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.940
Top Alpinist

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.940
(Attack)>Invites people he likes
to the mountains
(pretty tall ones)

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:47.580
We had full media coverage ready,
demonstration board commentary,

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.580
but then that moron Shimada...

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.420
Somebody must be talking about me.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:59.130
Even though he already lost once,
he just couldn't take the hint.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.510
Like an underdog, he clawed his way back up,

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:06.220
and then, in the third match to determine
the challenger, he crushed it with an upset win.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.890
It's like, would you give me a break?

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:13.270
B-But Mr. Shimada has been
making an incredible effort too, um...

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:13.270
(The voice of a Shimada fan)

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:17.020
Just imagining what the posters might be like
gets me down.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.940
KISHOU CHAMPIONSHIP
FIRST MATCH

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:26.280
MENTAL IMAGE

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.940
Could it be any drabber?

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.650
The close-up profiles of two homely old men...

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.280
I wouldn't even want to go!

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.280
Yeah, I can picture it.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:33.960
My heart won't even throb one bit.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:39.790
He's not young or flashy,
but his playing is strong and tenacious.

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:41.800
It doesn't have a single thing going for it.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:45.220
I have a feeling someone's saying
terrible things about me.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:49.430
If people don't talk about this event,
we'll lose sponsors.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.640
The Kishou Championship will be canceled.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.270
Well, yeah, reality is harsh.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:57.350
TURN

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.230
So you're doing us a solid here, Kiriyama!

00:05:58.560 --> 00:05:59.860
Good luck!

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:00.980
Doing you...

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:02.860
...a solid?

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.610
It means we're counting on you!

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:11.740
Hey, Kiriyama, what's wrong?

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:13.120
You suddenly froze up.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:14.700
Your face is red.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:15.580
Are you hot?

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.960
SHOGI HALL

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.370
Want some barley tea?

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:28.090
<i>How did I get home that night?</i>

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:33.350
<i>All kinds of things went in and out of my head.</i>

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:38.100
<i>It felt like I was floating,
so it was hard to walk.</i>

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:45.190
<i>Even after I got in bed,</i>

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:51.370
<i>the lights reflected on the river kept glimmering
and swaying in front of my eyes.</i>

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:54.040
<i>Gently swaying...</i>

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.840
<i>And the next day...</i>

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.130
After School Shogi Science Club
Now in Session!!

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.130
Sorry for being late.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:07.720
Excuse me...

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:12.600
Congratulations, Newcomer King Kiriyama

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:17.850
Congratulations, Newcomer King Kiriyama

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.440
Okay, now I'd like to...

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:24.610
have a toast to Kiriyama,
for winning the title of Newcomer King.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.610
Cheers!

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.450
Thank you.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:35.740
And now I'll explain the menu, a cornucopia
of the Shogi Science Club's scientific successes.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.750
First, the soft drink we just made a toast with...

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.630
is homemade ginger ale!

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:45.630
We used fresh ginger
that was growing behind the gym.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:49.720
Next, Caspian Sea yogurt, we spared no effort
to grow it in the physics prep room's refrigerator.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:52.510
And freshly-gathered natto
with rice flour dumplings.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:55.760
Plum jam made from the plums
off the tree in front of the principal's office.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:57.390
And finally, of course, our ramune.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.270
WAFT

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:04.520
Still, you did great, Kiriyama.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:07.730
Man, Yamazaki was good!

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:10.530
But you really stuck it out, Kiriyama.

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:11.780
I'm impressed you endured that.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:15.780
Mr. Hayashida was watching the live internet
broadcast and he was so worked up over it.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:17.830
He was yelling and cheering.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.790
They were about to kick us out of Mec's.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.920
Of course I was excited!

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:27.090
It was a broadcast of my student's game,
with a title on the line!

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.510
What is this? It's pretty good.

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.300
What do you mean by "pretty"?

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:36.050
But still...

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:41.810
that Pawn to 7-5 was a cool move.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:46.310
I was on the edge of my seat there.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:50.610
I never thought we would get
a Newcomer King from the Shogi Science Club!

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:55.070
When I think about one of my comrades
is fighting a battle, I feel so proud!

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:59.660
I'm still not great at shogi,
but I got so nervous just watching!

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.870
What's up, Kiriyama?

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:07.670
Um... I need to go to the bathroom.

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.050
I bet their weird food
is giving you stomach pains!

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:10.920
How rude!

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.470
- Well, I mean...
- Sheesh!

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.690
<i>I wonder what this is.</i>

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:37.620
<i>When did I get here?</i>

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.620
<i>To this...</i>

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.750
<i>warm place.</i>

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:49.210
Dang it.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:53.630
It won't stop.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:56.340
And everyone's waiting for me...

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:59.680
<i>It means we're counting on you!</i>

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.100
<i>Congratulations. You worked really hard for it.</i>

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.730
<i>Rei, thank you.</i>

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:10.400
<i>I wonder if what I suddenly gained...</i>

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.610
<i>will be lost just as suddenly.</i>

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:25.750
<i>But for now, I'm just happy.</i>

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:29.040
<i>I'm so happy...</i>

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:36.840
<i>That's it.</i>

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:41.390
<i>Even if it all does eventually disappear,
I'll never forget.</i>

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:46.060
<i>I'll never forget there were days
when I was truly happy.</i>

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:54.440
There's Kiriyama. We meet again.
Even though we already said goodbye.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:57.570
Looks like he's concentrating
on choosing something.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:01.570
DIARY CORNER
"Preserve Your Memories"

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:01.570
How embarrassing!

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:03.990
L-Let's leave him be!

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.750
It's the first page in the springtime of his life.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.080
Come on, let's go.

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:10.380
Well, I think I'll get one too.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:11.290
Hey!

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:12.790
Noguchi!

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:19.510
Maybe I'll go with this ten-year one.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:28.270
<i>So I can take it out and remember anytime,
any number of times.</i>

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:34.020
Where the Sun Shines

00:11:35.780 --> 00:11:38.030
Small World

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.790
Here. You should drink this.

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:57.380
It'll warm you up.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:00.220
Take it.

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:05.970
Th-Thank you.

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:08.390
Here, sit up a little more.

00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:10.440
You'll get burned if it spills on you.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.190
Sorry.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:23.910
If only I hadn't gotten sick,
we'd be off the mountain by now.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:27.330
I've been a drag on you all this time.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.910
And I've become
such a nuisance to you, Gakuto.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:31.920
You're not a nuisance.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:37.920
In the mountains, we have to bear
the burden of each other's lives.

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:43.050
If I didn't think you were up for that,
I would never have invited you.

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:48.180
That aside, I'm moved
by the tenacity you displayed today.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:53.310
You put up a nice fight, Issa.

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:57.190
Gakuto-senpai...

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:07.780
He taught me something that day.

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:08.240
SHOGI HALL

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:12.160
He taught me that the most important thing
is to not give up.

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:13.710
So...

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:19.380
I think Gakuto-senpai will become
the challenger for the Kishou Championship.

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:20.130
PLAINLY

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:23.430
Damn it. He's totally brainwashed.

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:26.640
As expected from the fearful
Sakurai 7th-Dan's mountain therapy.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:28.760
Issa is innocent, so he was done in one hit.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:30.890
Issa...

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:36.520
He invites people he likes or his rivals
to the mountains,

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:38.900
gets them in a jam,
and then treats them with kindness,

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.320
thereby gaining their trust.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:43.030
And the thing is, it's natural!
He has no evil intentions.

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:45.530
Gakuto Sakurai
Age 30
Class B-1

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:45.530
His refined behavior and kind smile
make him the number one favorite
in the shogi world.

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:45.530
That's scary! Gakuto is scary!

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:50.790
Once he's got you surrounded by mountains,
he takes over your mind completely.

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:52.290
Look at Issa.

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:58.790
FLUFF
FLUFF

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:56.330
At this rate, he probably can't beat
Sakurai in a match.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:58.790
Gakuto-senpai, good luck!

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.880
I hear Gakuto has invited
Mr. Shimada before, too.

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:03.880
Seriously?

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:06.220
Except...

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:09.100
The mountains, eh?

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:11.100
I've had my fill of the mountains.

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:11.100
STAB

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:11.100
HAHAHA

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:14.020
MIDDLE SCHOOL STUDENT

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:16.350
Ever since I was a little kid,
I got dropped off in the mountains

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:17.350
PACK

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:21.440
and told not to come back home until I filled up
my pack with bamboo shoots and vegetables.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:18.860
ROCK CLIMBING
IN SWEAT PANTS

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.110
<i>That was close!</i>

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:29.530
How can I put it?
That was part of my daily life.

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:31.830
So I think I've had enough of it.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:34.700
Really? That's too bad.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.790
That's Shimada 8th-Dan for you,
a natural-born mountain climber!

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:41.710
So cool! A man with a heart
that not even a therapist can access!

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:44.960
He's starting to move.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:56.520
Loose Stone Trap!

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:05.320
<i>But if I took that,</i>

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:09.410
<i>he would take my pawn at 4-2.</i>

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:14.740
<i>If I went with the same, upper gold general,
he would capture my 9-7 bishop.</i>

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:17.660
<i>Even promoting my rook and going to 8-9,</i>

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:22.250
<i>he would move his Bishop to 4-2
and get promoted,</i>

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:24.250
DRAGON HORSE

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:24.250
<i>and I'd be crushed.</i>

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:32.010
<i>In that case, I'll just move
my bishop to 8-9, promoted.</i>

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:36.310
I see.

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:38.640
Then...

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:47.990
RUMBLE
RUMBLE
CRASH

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:47.990
Falling Rocks Special!

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:21.390
Man, I'm tired.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.860
I need to take a little break.

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:25.770
That's our Shimada 8th-Dan!

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:29.400
He handles even an avalanche of powerful pieces
with his usual aplomb! So cool!

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.740
Gakuto will be okay, right?

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:37.200
But it would be better if Sakurai 7th-Dan wins,
so we can get more readers!

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:39.250
Please don't say that.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:41.080
I know, I shouldn't...

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:44.750
What? It looks like Shimada is going to win?

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.250
Saku, keep your voice down!

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:49.130
Don't do this to me!

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:52.180
Seriously, no one will come
to the Kishou Championship!

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:54.760
Shimada, let's take a hint here!

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:00.180
It's not over! We don't know yet!

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:03.730
Gakuto-senpai never gives up and right now,
his determination will cover the board...

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:09.530
No, we know.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:12.200
He uses his pawn at 5-1,
then after the same, Dragon,

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:14.780
he captures the 4-8 pawn
and gold general.

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:18.280
He's in trouble with the same,
upper gold general and lance at 4-5.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:21.160
The pawn is about to be promoted,
so he's got no defense.

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:25.920
Shimada is the challenger.

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:28.420
Come on, Toku, let's go drinking.

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:29.340
Sure!

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:37.180
The Kishou Championship,
my tenth win is on the line...

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:39.430
and my opponent is Shimada.

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:42.890
Sakurai has a bright personality,
and he's still green.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:45.400
He would've been the perfect opponent for me.

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:48.270
Well, things don't always go
the way you want them to.

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:53.190
<i>I'm sure if you leave Shimada alone,
he'll just start winning again.</i>

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:55.450
Gotou was right.

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:57.700
He doesn't have charm,

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:03.120
but he's bulked up some more,
and came back to us.

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:06.210
My tenth go-round
with the Kishou Championship.

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:10.920
I've better literally defend it to the death.

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:24.480
I did it! I won the challenger's right!

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:26.730
It brings me shivers!

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:30.320
And not metaphorically...

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:33.320
Ow... My stomach...

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.070
After School Shogi Science Club
Now in Session!!

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:40.160
<i>How could I have forgotten?</i>

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:44.250
Huh? Retiring?

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:45.960
That's right.

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:48.960
TWIRL TWIRL
TWIST TWIST

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:53.960
Trying to make straw sandals
with the straw gathered
from last year's rice crop
(for summer sandals)

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:50.380
After all, Kiriyama, other than you,
we're all third-years,

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.670
3RD-YEARS

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:53.960
so after summer vacation is over,
we have to focus on university entrance exams.

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:01.140
I... see.

00:19:03.970 --> 00:19:07.480
After all, you're all third-years.

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:15.240
<i>And so, just like that, I lost the one place
in school where I belonged.</i>

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:19.280
Is Kiriyama going to be okay?

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:23.490
He's gotten a little more
cheerful lately, but now this.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.250
You worry too much.

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:31.670
"Gaining" and "losing" things
are an unavoidable part of life for everyone.

00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:35.510
You feel joy, you feel disappointment,
and it repeats.

00:19:35.510 --> 00:19:39.380
And that's how you learn
how to handle your feelings.

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:44.810
Disappointment and loneliness
are necessary emotions.

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:48.770
Because of loneliness,
people muster courage...

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.940
and reach out to a new world.

00:19:53.820 --> 00:20:02.200
Doing that is like reaching out as a baby does,
and expands its small world.

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:05.160
GRAB

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.830
Teacher!

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.330
I'm a student.

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:10.370
THE NEXT DAY

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:12.380
Huh? Me?

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:14.130
I'll be fine.

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:17.960
Even alone, I can go over game records,
examine past data,

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:21.010
come up with strategies for my next match,
solve tsume-shogi problems...

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:24.470
Fully intending
on holing up inside school
(Too much sadness
made him throw away logic.)

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:24.470
HEAPS...

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:24.470
Hey, somebody get me paper and a marker!

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:28.020
I-I said I'm fine!

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:30.850
Honestly, there's a ton of stuff
I can do by myself.

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:34.270
Like researching new players
or coming up with countermeasures...

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:36.020
That's not what a club is!

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:36.020
SHOGI CLUB
COME JOIN!

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:39.780
Let's put up the new member
recruitment poster! Come on!

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:41.030
STUDENT COUNCIL

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:43.240
Huh, Shogi Science Club?

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:45.280
I didn't know we even had that.

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:48.540
You're looking for members now?
That's probably a tall order.

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:50.660
Went to Student Council
to get stamp of approval

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:50.660
I've never done it myself.

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:52.790
Well, you have my blessing.

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:52.790
Komahashi High School
Student Council Seal

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:54.420
Here. Good luck.

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:56.290
- Thanks.
- Right?

00:20:57.130 --> 00:21:00.470
<i>However, the issue was soon resolved.</i>

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:04.300
Kiriyama! Some people
who want to join the club are here!

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:09.140
They saw your poster.

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:11.690
Good gracious, isn't this amazing, Kiriyama?

00:21:12.390 --> 00:21:14.940
Um... I believe...

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:19.690
...you're the principal and vice-principal, right?

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:20.610
Actually...

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:27.620
Ever since you transferred here,
I wanted to have you teach me shogi!

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:32.040
I kept sending Hayashida
requests to join the Shogi Club...

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:36.880
but it was exasperating because he would
always say, "Right now is a little..."

00:21:37.090 --> 00:21:41.510
That's because Kiriyama didn't want
his professional status to be public.

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:46.470
Also, the head teacher, Nakamura,
said he wants to join too.

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:47.260
Thanks so much!

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:49.930
You did it, Kiriyama!

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:52.140
Including Mr. Hayashida,
you've got five members.

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:54.190
You can continue on as the Shogi Club alone!

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:56.520
And they're all bigwigs!

00:21:56.900 --> 00:22:01.280
B-But, um, clubs are supposed to have
at least five student members...

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:05.530
That's trivial! Kiriyama,
do you know who this man is?

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:07.280
He's the principal!

00:22:07.280 --> 00:22:10.830
So getting around these things is easy peasy.

00:22:10.830 --> 00:22:15.920
Well, I would like to put my own stamp on
the academy in a positive way, you know?

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:22.380
And I'd like our Hashi High team to make B class
in the Career Group Shogi Competition.

00:22:22.380 --> 00:22:25.720
That's definitely within our range.

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:28.930
And now we have acquired
the ultimate coach.

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:35.810
<i>Hasn't this now become
more of a shogi class than a shogi club?</i>

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:41.570
<i>And so, with the admission of a few unexpected
new members, the club can now continue!</i>

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:47.110
<i>A new adventure begins for Rei Kiriyama
and the jolly members.</i>

00:22:47.280 --> 00:22:48.030
Shogi Science Club
Now in Session!

00:22:47.610 --> 00:22:49.490
<i>One summer afternoon,
with the science division gone,</i>

00:22:49.070 --> 00:22:51.410
Shogi Club
*Currently Looking for Student Members

00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:53.200
<i>the Shogi Science Club
simply became the Shogi Club</i>

00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:57.290
<i>and the average member age
increased to 24 years old.</i>

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:00.040
Small World

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:37.600
Episode 34

00:24:32.340 --> 00:24:34.970
It's gone. It's gone. It's gone!

00:24:35.310 --> 00:24:39.270
Why does this
keep happening lately?

00:24:39.270 --> 00:24:40.640
Brown-noser...

00:24:40.640 --> 00:24:42.400
Did you think I would hit you?

00:24:42.400 --> 00:24:45.610
Teacher, do you believe that I hid it?

00:24:45.770 --> 00:24:47.730
Be it a parent-teacher conference,
or whatever,

00:24:47.730 --> 00:24:50.030
I'll always be on your side, Hina.

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:59.040
ILLUSTRATION:
HYOGONOSUKE

00:24:50.900 --> 00:24:53.950
Issa, the mountains aren't going
to get any bigger,

00:24:53.950 --> 00:24:56.080
but we have
a lot of room to grow.

00:24:56.080 --> 00:24:57.990
Yes, Gakuto-senpai!
